Hi Andrew and Tait,

Sorry for the long delay in looking into this. It turns out that the routine for reading those matrix sections from Mplus output was not handling the Fortran-style scientific notation (e.g., 1.225D-03) where the D is similar to the usual e in scientific notation, but explicitly denotes a double-formatted number. Anyhow, it's a Fortranism that I had seen, but hadn't thought about in text file parsing. I changed the routine so that any matrix-style output section now supports this D notation.

I have committed the update to Github, so you can install the development version to get the fix.

Best,
Michael

